description:
Phase 3: synthetic rule tests, one file per checker, following `test_quotes.py`
(13 synthetic cases, 0 mutant lambdas, 0 literal needles). A synthetic test feeds the
rule a case the rule must handle and a case it must reject, with no corpus read — so
the rule is tested on shapes the corpus may not contain.

This bead takes the **scanner and range** class:
- the paren-balanced link scanner against `[^)]*`: `preprints/Sharp-integral-fillings-in-CAT(0)-spaces-September-23-2026/paper.pdf` must resolve, and `[^)]*` must truncate it and invent a broken link;
- the strict paren class `preprints/(?:[^\s(){}\\]|\([0-9]+\))*\.pdf` gives 719 distinct matches, 0 absent from disk; the loose class (excluding only `\s` and parentheses) reads 717 distinct, 1 of which is not a file, and loses 2 real paths;
- a blank line at the end of a `path:a-b` range;
- a reversed range (`path:9-3`);
- a range that runs past the end of the file;
- the `read_file` line-label offset: a `read_file` label is one below the checker's `splitlines()` numbering, so a test that quotes a label must resolve to the checker's line.

Files: `test_index_links.py` (the scanner test exists; add the loose-class case),
`test_named_results.py`, `test_counterexample_crosscheck.py`,
`test_upstream_history.py`, `test_sources.py`, `test_faithfulness.py`.

Acceptance: each file has synthetic cases that pass against the shipped rule and fail
against the naive variant; no case reads the corpus; the gate reports 0 failures.

One row per relation type: edge type, source file, source line or pattern, count, and what the
edge does NOT mean. This is the typed-edge inventory the index schema decision needs.

Types measured 2026-10-07: family->manuscript 722; manuscript->formalized 162 of 722;
scope note->comparator statement 415 rows; family->main_results declaration 185 entries over 178
configs in 168 families; formalization->external lib 30 declared / 11 observed;
manuscript->bibliography 12,928 entries; abstract->"result NNN" 2; manuscript->manuscript 14 of
372 families; family->trace 10.

Negatives to record explicitly so no later pass re-derives them: 2 companion edges
(notes/scripts/build_catalog.py:267 defines the pattern, :288 the column; targets 032 and 006);
14 of 372 families have their own title phrase in any .bib; 0 MSC codes anywhere in the repo;
0 bib keywords fields; \keywords in only 12 of 722 manuscripts.

Acceptance: every count in the file is reproducible by a command listed in the row; the three name
relations (named-in-title, cited-in-bib, mentioned-in-body) are three separate rows, not one.
